From: Ethan Blanch <ethan.blanch@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:05:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] reg: read the ARM Thumb bit without bionic-only names

get_systrap_size() used ARM_cpsr and PSR_T_BIT, which only bionic headers
define, so the armv7 build fails against glibc. Use uregs[16] (CPSR) and
0x20 (the Thumb bit), which mean the same on both libcs.
---
diff --git a/src/tracee/reg.c b/src/tracee/reg.c
index 3859f8e..f0f3d37 100644
--- a/src/tracee/reg.c
+++ b/src/tracee/reg.c
@@ -383,8 +383,12 @@ int push_regs(Tracee *tracee) {
 
 word_t get_systrap_size(Tracee *tracee) {
 #if defined(ARCH_ARM_EABI)
-	/* On ARM thumb mode systrap size is 2 */
-	if (tracee->_regs[CURRENT].ARM_cpsr & PSR_T_BIT) {
+	/* On ARM thumb mode systrap size is 2.
+	 * Modified 2026-09-26 for uls-proot (github.com/ItsPhysip/uls-proot):
+	 * ARM_cpsr and PSR_T_BIT are bionic-only names.  Both bionic and glibc
+	 * define struct user_regs as uregs[18] with CPSR at index 16, and 0x20
+	 * is the CPSR Thumb bit. */
+	if (tracee->_regs[CURRENT].uregs[16] & 0x20) {
 		return 2;
 	}
 #elif defined(ARCH_ARM64)
